    tagline: "Tower-like limestone peaks, caves and lazy rivers", places: "Guilin · Yangshuo · Yunnan Stone Forest",
    intro: "Karst is the landscape you already know — the cone-shaped limestone peaks rising out of jade-green rivers that appear on every Chinese painting and banknote. It forms when mildly acidic rainwater slowly dissolves soluble limestone over millions of years, leaving behind towers, caves and underground rivers.",
